{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"**Decision: how should the tickets store reclaim unreachable objects and reflog — on a write-locked cadence that pauses writes, or not at all?**\n\nMeasured on the production tickets clone (`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, i-00880b2c7f13527c5, git 2.50.1, 2 vCPU) on 2026-11-11 ~22:45 PST, read-only:\n- `git prune -n --expire=2.weeks.ago` took 113.6 s; `--expire=now` took 107.1 s. Both report 28 unreachable objects. The store holds 1,070,683 packed objects and 50 loose objects. The cost is the reachability walk, not the deletion, so a real prune costs about the same.\n- The step's bound is 120 s (`_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT`); a prune would hold the write lock for ~110 s, blocking every ticket write host-wide for that long, and would be reaped by the bound on any slower day.\n- `.git/logs/HEAD` is 4.69 MB / 25,933 entries. On the local 1.13M-object repo, `git reflog expire --dry-run --all` took 0.28 s, so reflog expiry is cheap enough for the existing write-locked step.\n- The description's \"about 1,800 unreachable loose objects\" no longer matches: today 28 objects are unreachable.\n- The 2 stale doc passages (`docs/concurrency.md` caveat, `docs/scale-envelope.md` §\"Git maintenance & gc\") need fixing in every branch.\n\nHow should unreachable-object and reflog growth be handled?\n(1) **Add reflog expiry to the write-locked maintenance step (cheap, every run that triggers), record unreachable-object growth as accepted at the measured rate with an operator-run prune via `rebar store maintenance` as the remedy, and fix both docs**\n(2) Add reflog expiry plus a write-locked prune at a fixed cadence (e.g. weekly), accepting a ~110 s global write pause each time, and fix both docs\n(3) Record both growths as accepted at the measured rate, change no code, and fix both docs\n\nWork moved on to the next queued bug pending this answer; the ticket stays open and unclaimed.\n"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794466259853591001,"uuid":"1a69e69c-e6f5-4b60-ad44-5de13e5c2446"}